  {"id":"acid-base-cc-2","topic":"Acid-Base Disorders in Critical Care","domain":"Anesthesia critical care (shock & resuscitation, sepsis, ARDS & mechanical ventilation, hemodynamic monitoring, AKI, sedation/delirium, nutrition, end-of-life)","discipline":"anesthesia","stem":"If pH and PaCO2 both change in the same direction, what is the primary disorder?","answer":"Primary metabolic disorder (both change together); if they change in opposite directions, the primary disorder is respiratory.","rationale":"pH and PaCO2 change in opposite directions in respiratory disorders; same-direction change indicates metabolic primary with respiratory compensation.","bloom":"analyze","source":[{"book":"Marino ICU Book","page":372}],"confusable_with":""},
